# Indirect Geospatial Referencing through Place Names in the Digital Library: Alexandria Digital Library Experience with Developing and Implementing Gazetteers.

**Authors:** Hill, Linda L., Zheng, Qi

## Abstract
Describes the development by the Alexandria Digital Library of a gazetteer (dictionary of geographic names) composed of a Gazetteer Content Standard, a Feature Type Thesaurus, and an operational interactive gazetteer service. Illustrates the use of this tool in a georeferenced digital library and relates progress in working with Federal agencies and others toward developing sharable gazetteer data. (AEF)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ597560

